DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       ttggaattooppppmm reads a TrueVision Targa file as input and produces a PPM  im‐
       age as output.


OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       In  addition  to  the options common to all programs based on libnetpbm
       (most notably --qquuiieett, see
        Common Options ⟨index.html#commonoptions⟩ ), ttggaattooppppmm  recognizes  the
       following command line options:

       All options can be abbreviated to their shortest unique prefix.




       ----aallpphhaaoouutt==_a_l_p_h_a_-_f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e
              ttggaattooppppmm   creates a PGM image containing the transparency chan‐
              nel values in the input image.  If the input image doesn't  con‐
              tain  a  transparency  channel, the _a_l_p_h_a_-_f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e file contains
              all zero (transparent) transparency values.  If you don't  spec‐
              ify ----aallpphhaaoouutt, ttggaattooppppmm does not generate an alpha file, and if
              the input image has a transparency channel, ttggaattooppppmm simply dis‐
              cards it.

              If  you specify -- as the filename, ttggaattooppppmm writes the transpar‐
              ency output to Standard Output and discards the image.

              See ppaammccoommpp(1) for one way to use the transparency output file.


       ----hheeaaddeerrdduummpp
              Causes ttggaattooppppmm to dump information from the TGA header to Stan‐
              dard Error.




